\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Bondi's sign rules for two bodies released from rest, after Forward~\cite  {forward1990}. Every body has positive inertial and passive mass; the active mass of the dashed bodies is negative. (a)~Two positive masses attract and (b)~two negative masses repel; in both cases the forces are opposite and the barycentre stays at rest. (c)~For a positive and a negative mass both forces point the same way, so the pair accelerates while its total momentum stays zero.}}{1}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:schematic}{{1}{1}{Bondi's sign rules for two bodies released from rest, after Forward~\cite {forward1990}. Every body has positive inertial and passive mass; the active mass of the dashed bodies is negative. (a)~Two positive masses attract and (b)~two negative masses repel; in both cases the forces are opposite and the barycentre stays at rest. (c)~For a positive and a negative mass both forces point the same way, so the pair accelerates while its total momentum stays zero}{figure.1}{}}
