\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces (a)~$\Delta X$ of PM10 at $N=128$, 192 and 256, and of the $N=128$ simulations with a 4.4 times tighter elliptic-solver tolerance (PM10-tol, circles) and with mesh refinement allowed (PM10-AMR, crosses). Inset: the end of the run. (b)~$L_2$ norm of the Hamiltonian constraint over the whole domain, at $t=0$ and averaged over $t\ge 150$, against $\Delta x$; the $t=0$ values are dominated by the cells next to the outer boundary (Appendix~\ref {app:constraints}). The two highest resolutions agree to $0.4\%$ in $\Delta X(200)$, and $N=128$ lies $4\%$ below.}}{11}{figure.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:convergence}{{9}{11}{(a)~$\Delta X$ of PM10 at $N=128$, 192 and 256, and of the $N=128$ simulations with a 4.4 times tighter elliptic-solver tolerance (PM10-tol, circles) and with mesh refinement allowed (PM10-AMR, crosses). Inset: the end of the run. (b)~$L_2$ norm of the Hamiltonian constraint over the whole domain, at $t=0$ and averaged over $t\ge 150$, against $\Delta x$; the $t=0$ values are dominated by the cells next to the outer boundary (Appendix~\ref {app:constraints}). The two highest resolutions agree to $0.4\%$ in $\Delta X(200)$, and $N=128$ lies $4\%$ below}{figure.9}{}}
